    "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\n`split_list(..., contiguous=False)` converts its input to a NumPy array before splitting it. This can change element types (`[1, 'two']` becomes strings), turn tuples into lists, or raise `ValueError` for nested lists of different lengths.\n\nUse stepped list slices to preserve the original elements and their identities while keeping the existing round-robin order. The contiguous path is unchanged.\n\nAdd seven regression and compatibility tests covering mixed types, ragged lists, tuple identity, both splitting modes, empty inputs, and more shards than items.\n\n## Experiment results\n\nOn macOS arm64, Python 3.11.15, NumPy 1.26.4:\n\n- Before the fix, `python -m pytest tests/utils/test_split_list.py -q`: **3 failed, 4 passed**.\n- After the fix, `python -m pytest tests/utils/test_split_list.py tests/utils/test_format_time.py tests/utils/test_io_utils.py tests/utils/test_file_utils.py -q`: **17 passed**.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: all ten hooks passed.\n\nNo GPU or model downloads were needed. Full training and distributed checkpoint integration tests were not run.\n\nThis patch and its tests were prepared with Codex assistance.\n",
